From 762844df73e10d8afcabb51c5d4bcbf8dec88814 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:15:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_tasks_panel: delete archived task records

The Agent Tasks panel of 0035 could archive and unarchive a task record
but never remove one, so the Archived filter only grew: every task the
agent ever ran stayed there until the user deleted Zeo's data. Story 025.

An archived row now carries Delete (a trash icon, "Delete This Record")
beside Unarchive, and with the Archived filter on the filter bar offers
"Delete All Archived" while there is something archived to delete. Both
ask first -- "Delete N task records? The threads are not affected." --
with Delete and Cancel, the way the card's Stop does; Cancel does
nothing. Delete All deletes the batch the prompt counted, so a task
archived while the prompt is open is not deleted unasked.

Only an archived record can be deleted. A running task is never archived
(0035 R3.4), and the statement itself is guarded: DELETE ... WHERE
session_id = ? AND task_id = ? AND archived = 1, one savepoint per batch,
so a key that is not archived is left in place and a failure part-way
keeps every row of the batch. The thread is never touched: deleting
removes the history row only -- not the thread, its metadata, or its
transcript.

Memory changes first and keeps the deletion when the write fails, which
is logged once with every session and task id -- the same contract as
archiving. A deleted key is also remembered for the rest of the session,
because the feed keeps repeating a finished task while its thread is
open, and without it the record would be written again on the next
snapshot. The remembering is session-only by design: a column or table
for it would be a migration, and this patch adds none. A thread reopened
after a restart whose agent still lists the task can therefore record it
again, as a new, unarchived row.

No migration, no setting, no new dependency. Rides claude-agent-acp-plus
BY DEPENDENCY after 0041, like 0035 itself: the history is fed only by
0037's card.

Fixed 2026-10-09 (0.2.2_p20261009), in this patch because it is the last to touch the history
row decoder: one row whose status this build cannot read -- a newer Zeo wrote it,
an older one opened the database -- failed `load_all`, so the whole history went
Unavailable and `queue_write` dropped every write for the session. The decoder now
yields the row or why it is unreadable; `load_all` skips the unreadable ones with a
warning naming session/task and status, and the row stays for the build that
understands it. Tests at both levels (`load_all`, and the store staying Available
and still writing), each failing without the fix.

Tests added (0.2.3_p20261009): delete-all removes exactly the counted batch still archived
-- not a row unarchived while the prompt was open, not one archived after the
count -- checked in the store's memory as well as the database; and a delete
batch is atomic when a row fails mid-way.
---

